    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42630" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sardĭus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		cf. 1. sarda, II., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>sardian</i>, <i>carnelian</i> (late
			Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lapis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Exod. 28, 17</span></i>
			.—Hence, <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sardĭus</span></b> ,
			ii, m., <i>the
			carnelian</i>, <i>a precious stone</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Exod.
				39, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Apoc. 21, 20</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 2, 10</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">called lapis sardinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Apoc. 4, 3</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Hier. in Isa. 15, 54, v. 11
			sq.</span></i></div>
